---
import { ROLES } from '@lib/features/issue-tracking';
---

<section class="border-t border-line bg-app" aria-labelledby="safeguards-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <h2 id="safeguards-title" class="h2">
        Five roles, and a way back from mistakes.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5 max-w-[46ch]">
        There are no permission schemes to design. Each person has a role in each project, an agent can never do more
        than the person it acts for, and the same rules hold in the app, the API and MCP.
      </p>
      <dl class="scopes mt-8">
        {ROLES.map(item => (
          <>
            <dt>{item.role}</dt>
            <dd>{item.can}</dd>
          </>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7 rule-list">
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="h3">Deleted, then restorable for 14 days.</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          A Project Admin confirms the delete and the issue leaves the project at once. For 14 days it comes back from
          the Undo that follows or from the project’s list of deleted issues, with its comments, time, files and
          history.
        </p>
        <p class="quote mt-3">ACME-12 deleted · Undo</p>
      </div>
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="h3">People who leave keep their name.</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          Everything a former colleague did keeps their real name and picture, with a <em>Former member</em> label,
          never “Deleted user”. Their work stays searchable.
        </p>
        <p class="quote mt-3">created by: @alex</p>
      </div>
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="h3">Issues leave as CSV whenever you like.</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          Export any list exactly as searched and sorted, up to 10,000 issues, with the columns you choose, custom
          fields included. Issues come in from any CSV, with a column mapping and a dry run first. There is no native
          importer from another tracker.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
